    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Make the best five-card poker hand using Deuces as wild cards. In Diablo mode, the opener must win the pot or match it to fund the next hand.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Ante: Standard ante from all players.\n2. Deal: 5 cards to each player.\n3. First Betting Round: Standard poker betting begun by player to dealer's left.\n4. The Draw: Active players may discard and draw a MAXIMUM of two cards.\n5. Second Betting Round: Standard betting begun by the player who opened the first round.\n6. Showdown: Best hand wins the pot.\n7. Diablo rule: If the opener does not win, the opener contributes an amount equal to the just-won pot to seed the next hand. Deal passes left and the next hand is played with no new antes. The cycle continues until a hand in which the opener wins.",
      "Scoring example: Pot-based cash game. Winner of each hand takes the pot. Diablo mechanism creates escalating pots. Player with highest 5-card poker hand at showdown wins the current pot. If the opener loses, the opener matches the just-won pot to create the next hand's carryover pot..",
